1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,615
White light is a mixture of all colours. When it enters a glass prism, it slows down and bends.

2
00:00:05,615 --> 00:00:08,832
But each colour travels at a slightly different speed,

3
00:00:08,832 --> 00:00:13,218
so each bends by a different amount: violet and blue bend most, red least.

4
00:00:13,218 --> 00:00:17,079
The colours spread out into a spectrum. This is called dispersion.

5
00:00:18,137 --> 00:00:24,629
Rainbows form the same way. Sunlight is refracted as it enters a raindrop, reflected off the back of the drop,

6
00:00:24,629 --> 00:00:29,484
and refracted again as it leaves, splitting white light into a spectrum of colours.
